.TH "git-enhance" 1

.SH NAME
git-enhance - configure a checkout with the enhancements available for its repo

.SH SYNOPSIS
git enhance [--force]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Finds the enhancements that correspond to the current repo, writes the files
that enable them in the current worktree, and removes files it previously wrote
for enhancements that no longer apply. Running it again with nothing changed
does nothing, so it is safe to run at any time.

The repo name is the first path component under ~/repos of the main checkout,
found through the common git directory so that linked worktrees resolve to
their repo wherever they live. For example ~/repos/dart-sdk/sdk is
"dart-sdk". Checkouts outside of ~/repos have no enhancements, and bare
repositories are skipped.

.SH ENHANCEMENTS
.TP
Dev shells
If ~/repos/dotfiles/dev-shells/<repo>.nix exists, writes .envrc to use that
shell from the dotfiles flake with \fBuse flake\fR, and runs \fBdirenv allow\fR
on it. The file starts with \fBsource_up_if_exists\fR so an .envrc above the
checkout still loads. New files in dev-shells must be added to git before the
flake can see them.
.TP
Agent skills
If ~/.vibes/skills/repos/<repo> is a directory, hardlinks each skill directory
under it into .agents/skills/<skill>, adds a managed block in
\&.git/info/exclude so git ignores those directories in every worktree of the
repo, and removes any legacy ~/.vibes/skills/repos entries from
\&.agents/skills.json. Hardlinks stay inside the workspace root (satisfying
coding-agent workspace path confinement, which rejects external skills.json
paths and symlinks) and share inodes with ~/.vibes so in-place edits show up
immediately; editors that save atomically by renaming a temp file break the
link, in which case rerunning \fBgit enhance\fR relinks it (with \fB--force\fR
if SKILL.md itself was replaced).

.SH OWNERSHIP
An .envrc written by git enhance starts with a "Generated by git-enhance"
comment, and is rewritten or removed freely, so don't edit it by hand. A skill
directory in .agents/skills/<skill> belongs to git enhance when its SKILL.md
shares an inode with a skill under ~/.vibes/skills/repos; stale owned skill
directories are removed when a skill is renamed or deleted. If an .envrc
without that comment or an unowned .agents/skills/<skill> directory exists when
an enhancement applies, it is left alone and the command exits non-zero. Move
what it does into git enhance, or rerun with \fB--force\fR to replace it.

Files tracked by the repo are never modified, even with \fB--force\fR.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
-f, --force
Replace an .envrc or .agents/skills/<skill> directory not owned by git enhance.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
GIT_ENHANCE_REPOS, GIT_ENHANCE_DOTFILES, and GIT_ENHANCE_SKILLS override the
~/repos, ~/repos/dotfiles, and ~/.vibes/skills/repos paths.
